{Sicilian Dragon, 33 moves. When Broadbent and Wood sat down to play this
last-round game, they still had one adjourned game each to finish (Broadbent,
his 7th round game with Morry, and Wood his 10th round game with Milner-Barry).
Hence they both had 7/9 at the time.} 27. a6 Bg3 $19 28. Rf1 Qh4 $4 (28... Bh2+
29. Kxh2 Rxf1 30. Bf2 Qe7 $19 {and Baruch Wood would have been 1948 British
Champion}) 29. Rxf8+ Kxf8 30. a7 $18 Qh2+ 31. Kf1 {... 33 moves (Source: BCM,
Nov 1948, p379)} 1-0

